Exclude missing and explicitly invalid readings before taking the middle. Return median as an object property.
Python 3:
readings=[{'v':8,'ok':True},{'v':None,'ok':False},{'v':2,'ok':True},{'v':99,'ok':False},{'v':6,'ok':True}]
values=[]
for reading in readings:
    if reading['ok'] and reading['v'] is not None:
        values.append(reading['v'])
values=sorted(values)
result={'median':values[len(values)//2]}
Serialize result as exactly one JSON value.
